{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/142853-help-with-contracts-of-ice-ice-sculpting","id":142853,"title":"Help with Contracts of Ice/Ice Sculpting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-19T18:11:36-07:00","id":142853,"title":"Help with Contracts of Ice/Ice Sculpting","content":"Hi, I\u2019m new here and I'm looking at creating a Snowskin/Artist Ice sculptor who along with several other changelings was forced by their keeper to create sculptures of predatory animals from ice. Their keeper \u201cencouraged\u201d them by exempting the artist who most impressed her from punishments until after the next contest. The Keeper would animate the sculptures and use them to hunt the other changelings through frozen forests or force them to engage in mortal combat with their creations in an amphitheatre of ice.<br /> <br /> Though they obviously didn\u2019t harbour warm and fuzzy feelings for their keeper they truly enjoyed the challenge of creating these chilling works of art and were enchanted by their keeper\u2019s ability to bring their work to life.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m looking at having this character form a contract with either Ice or more specifically the shaping of Ice. I\u2019d much appreciate it if I could get some perspective from other fans of the game on my thoughts so far. Constructive criticism and suggestions would be very welcome. I'd also be interested in hearing alternate names for the clauses.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1: Possible Name: Biting Cold<br /> 1 Glamour<br /> The changeling can chill a weapon causing it to sap the warmth from the limbs of their foes. Mechanically this could manifest as mounting penalties to Speed and Initiative equal to the successes on the roll and to a maximum of five for the rest of the scene.<br /> On an exceptional success could last until the victim makes a significant effort to warm themselves such as huddling round a fire or taking a long hot shower.<br /> The Catch: The changeling applies this clause to a weapon made of Ice such as an icicle or a weapon created by the third clause of this Contract.<br /> Modelled somewhat after bite of the wooden fang as well as numerous clauses from the contracts of the Wild. An alternate version of this clause could emulate Bite of the Wooden Fang with Ice crystals or small Icicles rather than Thorns however I'd prefer it to work with weapons which inflict lethal damage as well as those which inflict bashing damage.<br /> <br /> 2: Possible Name: Touch of Frost<br /> 1 Glamour<br /> The changeling can freeze a volume of a liquid.<br /> Quantities are taken from Control Elements. 1 success = a milk jug\u2019s worth, 2 = a petrol tank, 3 = a bathtub, 4 = average Jacuzzi, 5 = Large hot tub.<br /> The Catch: The changeling throws a pinch of salt over their shoulder when invoking this clause. This appeals to me as the changeling is discarding salt which is used to melt ice<br /> Modifiers could offer bonuses in low temperature environments and penalties when attempting to freeze a substance other than water e.g. coca cola or substances with low melting points e.g. petrol.<br /> This clause is a variation of Touch of Winter though instead of freezing the surface of a potentially large body of water the changeling freezes a reduced volume of the liquid completely.<br /> I\u2019m not certain whether this contract should be an instant or extended action.<br /> <br /> 3: Possible Name: Wintersmith<br /> 2 Glamour<br /> The Changeling can form an item or tool from ice, water or the air itself. This would allow the changeling to form a sword, chair or flight of stairs from Ice in just a few turns.<br /> This clause is taken straight out of Contracts of Ice from Kismet\u2019s World of Darkness. <a href=\"http://www.vtm.kismetrose.com/ctl/ContractIce.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.vtm.kismetrose.com/ctl/ContractIce.html</a><br /> The Catch: I\u2019m uncertain, possibly the inverse of Noonday Grasp e.g. swallowing the flame from a match?<br /> <br /> 4:Possible Name: White Knight (I'd really prefer a better name for this one, preferably something which continues the crafting theme) <br /> 3 Glamour<br /> The Changeling can breathe life into an ice sculpture bringing it to life temporarily.<br /> The sculpture can act as an ally much like the elemental created by the contract Elemental Servitor.<br /> The Catch: The Changeling has carved the sculpture with their own hands (tools are permitted but contracts are not) and presented it with an article of their own clothing e.g. a scarf, a ring or an old felt hat.<br /> This clause is based loosely on the song about frosty the snowman.<br /> <br /> <br /> This next clause is the one I am most uncertain about.<br /> <br /> 5: Possible Name: Frozen Hold<br /> 4 Glamour and an optional Willpower Point as in the contract Hedgewall<br /> The Changeling creates a structure from frozen water, from a looming wall of slippery ice to a palace formed from frost.<br /> This clause is based on Hedgewall with a few alterations. I want the character to be able to create an actual building from ice (more for flavour and rp purposes than combat ones e.g. creating a structure from ice at a court celebration). In practice I feel that if a structure with a roof is formed then it should come at the cost of the length of the walls (the same volume of ice but rearranged. If the length of the Walls is Wyrd x 10 Yards then the walls of the structure could be reduced in length to Wyrd x 5 yards?<br /> So a changeling with Wyrd four would be able to create a forty yard long wall or a structure with a walls of length 20 yards e.g. a 5x5 square structure or a circular tower with a circumference of 20 yards.<br /> Alternatively could the volume of ice be increased in regards to the inability to include the preceding 4 contracts into the structure to increase the power of the Clause as it is in the contracts of Thorn and Brambles.<br /> The Catch: The changeling shatters a mirror when they invoke this clause or alternately the changeling inflicts a point of lethal damage with a shard of broken mirror.<br /> The catch from this clause is based upon the story of the Snow Queen by Hans Christian Anderson.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019d very much prefer it if the clauses from this contract would remain in effect if used to shape existing ice rather than forming it so if they used existing snow and ice to create sculptures or structures in winter then they wouldn't melt until the weather changed and thaw began. It\u2019s my intention that this would be more for flavour than an advantage in game terms.Do you think this would be possible or overpowered compared with other contracts?<br /> 1: No effect?<br /> 2: If the environment is bellow the point where the liquid would naturally freeze then it will not thaw until the temperature rises. It would be unnatural if a block of ice suddenly melted in a freezer.<br /> 3: If this clause is used to sculpt an object from an existing block of ice then it remains until it melts under environmental conditions. If kept in a refrigerated room it may last indefinitely.<br /> 4: After the period of animation of the sculpture ends the sculpture remains frozen in place until it is once more animated or it melts due to environmental conditions e.g. fire, heating, the noonday sun.<br /> 5: The structure remains until it naturally melts e.g. when spring comes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3064,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3064-falconidae","user":"Falconidae","date":". 05-19-2014, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3064-falconidae","name":"Falconidae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}